 "checks": [
  "<b>Held-out test.</b> The habit model learns from Amazon's 6,112 training routes. Every number here is scored on the 3,052 evaluation routes Amazon held back.",
  "<b>Official metric.</b> Amazon score uses a port of the challenge scorer that matches the original exactly on 40 randomised test routes.",
  "<b>Solver quality.</b> On 200 routes our engine's shortest path (the code the browser runs) is 2.26% shorter than Google OR-Tools given 5 s per route, with a 0.3 s budget.",
  "<b>Ablation.</b> Our first engine saved 3.3% and drove longer than the driver on 18% of routes. Moving whole zones in the search and counting lateness when accepting a tour took that to 5.9% and 2.4%.",
  "<b>Uncertainty.</b> Drive time saved at the default setting: 5.9% (95% bootstrap interval 5.8% to 6.1%). Shortest path: 11.3% (11.2% to 11.5%).",
  "<b>Delivery windows.</b> 28,354 stops have a time window. Late stops: driver's order 469, Line of Travel 1.",
  "<b>No leakage.</b> Station-history features for a training route only count other days; evaluation routes only see training history.",
  "<b>Honest limit.</b> Travel times are Amazon's planned estimates, not GPS traces, so savings are measured in Amazon's own matrix. Drivers may know shortcuts the matrix does not."
 ],
